# p_census_peak_x2: diagnostic. Owner census at the true peak of the per-layer arm's last row (x2).
#
# reason     (1) recorder table covers 38% of x2's peak (430,672 of 1,139,484 kB), one named row
#            libc10.so+0x4a675 431.7 MB (torch allocator); (2) Python census fired at 74% (rss 845,688 kB;
#            PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT throttle). Run with PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT=0 (undecomposed program: 74.5% -> 97.9%).
# question   arm:
#              x0_per_layer_base   2,026,372     the decomposition alone
#              x1_per_layer        1,416,216     + six levers
#              x2_per_layer_disk   1,135,384     + the plaintext layers on disk
#            donor ladder exhausted except 04_reduce_temp (polynomial GELU: different function, outside
#            phase B). Hint: libc10.so+0x4a675 431.7 MB ~ the 433 MB payload.
# not a step probe_census_cpu records only; x2's six levers unchanged.
